			<div class=3D"entry_title" _msttexthash=3D"762151" _msthash=3D"5">Fracta=
l Adaptive Moving Average</div>
			<div class=3D"entry_body"><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"29266=
8506" _msthash=3D"6"> The fractal adaptive moving average is a type of <a h=
ref=3D"http://exceltechnical.web.fc2.com/ema.html" _mstmutation=3D"1" _istr=
anslated=3D"1">exponential moving average</a>. It was developed by John Ehl=
ers. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> It is characterized by cal=
culating the smoothing constant from the fractal dimension of the specified=
 period each time. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The smoothin=
g constant changes from calculation day to day, which is the same as <a hre=
f=3D"http://exceltechnical.web.fc2.com/vidya.html" _mstmutation=3D"1" _istr=
anslated=3D"1">VIDYA</a> and <a href=3D"http://exceltechnical.web.fc2.com/k=
ama.html" _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1">Kaufmann's adaptive moving=
 averages</a>. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The fractal dime=
nsion is closer to 1 closer to a straight line, and the larger the value is=
 when it is messy. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The smoothin=
g constant calculated from the fractal dimension is characterized by the fa=
ct that the closer the fractal dimension is to 1, the larger the value, so =
when the movement is<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> linear, it =
is asymptotic to the stock price, and in the case of a random movement, the=
 movement of the moving average is smaller.</font><br>
			<br>
			<div class=3D"formula_title" _msttexthash=3D"387348" _msthash=3D"7">Calc=
ulation formula</div>
			<div class=3D"formula"><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"21596378=
7" _msthash=3D"8"> Mid =3D (High + Low) =81=80 2 <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _is=
translated=3D"1"> MF =3D First half of the specified period (1~M/2)<br _mst=
mutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> MB =3D Second half of the specified per=
iod (M/2+1~M)<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> N1 =3D (Maximum va=
lue of Mid in MF period - Minimum value of Mid in MF period) =81=80 MF<br _=
mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> N2 =3D (Maximum value of Mid in MB p=
eriod - Minimum value of Mid in MB period) =81=80 MB<br _mstmutation=3D"1" =
_istranslated=3D"1"> N3 =3D (Maximum value of Mid in M period - Minimum val=
ue of Mid in M period) =81=80 M<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> =
D=3D(Log(N1+N2)-Log(N3))=81=80Log(2)<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D=
"1"> A=3DExp(-4.6*(D-1)) <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <b _ms=
tmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1">Fractal Adaptive Moving Average =3D Fra=
ctal Adaptive Moving Average of the previous day + (Close of the day - Frac=
tal Adaptive Moving Average of the previous day) =81~ A</b><br _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> M specifies <b _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=
=3D"1">an even number</b><br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Note 1=
: From day 1 ~ day M - 1 day, the fractal adaptive moving average =3D Mid v=
alue Note<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> 2: If A becomes 1 or m=
ore, A =3D 1</font><br>
			</div>

