			<div class=3D"entry_title" _msttexthash=3D"1937650" _msthash=3D"10">Use =
Excel to calculate fractal adaptive moving average</div><font _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"7933575" _msthash=3D"11"> This section describes the=
 procedure for calculating the Fractal Adaptive Moving Average using Excel.=
 <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istran=
slated=3D"1"> Functions to use </font><div class=3D"formula">
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"442520" _msthash=3D"12">MAX=
(number1,number2,...)</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"2982850=
" _msthash=3D"13"> Returns the maximum value from a specified number or a n=
umber in a range.</font><br>
				<br>
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"442182" _msthash=3D"14">MIN=
(number1,number2,...)</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"2997020=
" _msthash=3D"15"> Returns the minimum value from a specified number or a r=
ange of numbers.</font><br>
				<br>
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"341315" _msthash=3D"16">LOG=
(number,bottom)</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"9250345" _mst=
hash=3D"17"> Returns the logarithm of the number at the specified base. If =
the bottom is omitted, it is assumed that 10 is specified for the bottom.</=
font><br>
        <br>
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"152698" _msthash=3D"18">EXP=
 (number)</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"1021215" _msthash=
=3D"19"> Returns the power of a number based on e.</font><br>
        <br>
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"2664155" _msthash=3D"20">OF=
FSET(base cell,number of rows,number of columns,height,width)</div><font _m=
stmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"22683648" _msthash=3D"21"> Refers to the c=
ell that has been moved from the base cell by the specified number of rows =
and columns. Or, set the height and width to specify the cell range of the =
specified height and width from the reference cell.</font><br>
				<br>
				<br>
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"544557" _msthash=3D"22">IF(=
condition, true, false)</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"43924=
40" _msthash=3D"23"> Returns the true value if the expression is satisfied,=
 and the false value if it does not.</font><br>
				<br>
				<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"106873" _msthash=3D"24">ROW=
 (cell)</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"8130681" _msthash=3D"=
25"> Returns the row number of the cell. If nothing is specified, it return=
s the row number of the cell in which the ROW is written.</font><br>		=09
			</div>
			<br>
		=09
			<table width=3D"10%" height=3D"10%" border=3D"1" align=3D"center">
			<tbody><tr>
			<td><img src=3D"http://exceltechnical.web.fc2.com/image/eframa-01.gif"><=
/td>
			</tr>
			</tbody></table><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"634526503" _mst=
hash=3D"26"> The Fractal Adaptive Moving Average is calculated based on the=
 <a href=3D"http://exceltechnical.web.fc2.com/calcprice.html#midprice" _mst=
mutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1">midpoint (average of the highs and lows)=
</a> using the<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> fractal adaptive =
moving average of the previous day and the fractal dimension of the specifi=
ed period. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Here, we will use th=
e OFFSET function so that we can calculate the fractal adaptive moving aver=
age of any parameter. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstm=
utation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Since the fractal dimension value is req=
uired to calculate the fractal adaptive moving average, we will calculate i=
t first and then calculate the fractal adaptive moving average. <br _mstmut=
ation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"=
> The fractal dimension is calculated using the middle price (the average o=
f the high and low prices). <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Col=
umns F ~ J are the parts that calculate the fractal dimension. <br _mstmuta=
tion=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Calculate the smoothing constant in column =
K and the fractal adaptive moving average in column<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _=
istranslated=3D"1"> L. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mst=
mutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The L4 cell is the cell that specifies =
the number used to calculate the smoothing constant of the fractal adaptive=
 moving average. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutati=
on=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Calculate the middle price in the F column. F=
or an explanation of the calculation formula, see <a href=3D"http://excelte=
chnical.web.fc2.com/calcprice.html#midprice" _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslat=
ed=3D"1">the middle price</a>. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> =
<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Calculate MF <b _mstmutation=3D=
"1" _istranslated=3D"1">=81=80 N1 of the formula N1 (maximum value of Mid f=
or MF period - minimum value of Mid for MF period)</b> in column G. <br _ms=
tmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The formula is </font><div class=3D"ex=
celformula" _msttexthash=3D"2600169" _msthash=3D"27">
			(MAX(OFFSET(C5,-$L$4/2,0,-$L$4/2,1))-MIN(OFFSET(D5,-$L$4/2,0,-$L$4/2,1))=
)/($L$4/2)
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"89835005" _msthash=3D"28"=
> Are. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> In this column, the firs=
t half of the period is calculated, so the specified interval is 1~M/2. <br=
 _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> This part is specified by the OFFS=
ET function, but it is a little complicated, so please refer to the explana=
tion of <a href=3D"http://exceltechnical.web.fc2.com/excelfunction.html#off=
set" _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1">the OFFSET function</a> for how=
 to specify it. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutatio=
n=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> In column H, N2 of the formula is calculated. =
<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The shape of the formula is the=
 same as the G column, but the arguments in the OFFSET function are slightl=
y different. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The formula is</fo=
nt><br>
			<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"1962259" _msthash=3D"29">
			(MAX(OFFSET(C5,0,0,-$L$4/2,1))-MIN(OFFSET(D5,0,0,-$L$4/2,1)))/($L$4/2)
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"1942811" _msthash=3D"30">=
 Are. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _i=
stranslated=3D"1"> Column I calculates N3 of the formula. <br _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The formula is</font><br>
			<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"1606917" _msthash=3D"31">
			(MAX(OFFSET(C5,0,0,-$L$4,1))-MIN(OFFSET(D5,0,0,-$L$4,1)))/$L$4
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"16511885" _msthash=3D"32"=
> Are. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _=
istranslated=3D"1"> Calculate the fractal dimension in the J column. <br _m=
stmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Since the formula for calculating the=
 fractal dimension is <b _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1">(Log(N1+N2)=
-Log(N3))=81=80Log(2),</b> the formula to be entered in the<br _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> cell is </font><div class=3D"excelformula" _mst=
texthash=3D"425932" _msthash=3D"33">
			=3D(LOG(G5+H5)-LOG(I5))/LOG(2)
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"19925204" _msthash=3D"34"=
> It comes to. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> In column K, the smoothing constant is calculat=
ed using the fractal dimension calculated in column J. <br _mstmutation=3D"=
1" _istranslated=3D"1"><b _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1">Since the =
formula is defined as Exp(-4.6*(D-1)),</b> the formula to be entered in the=
<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> cell is</font><br>
			<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"154180" _msthash=3D"35">
			EXP(-4.6*(J5-1))
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"13591526" _msthash=3D"36"=
> However, if this value is 1 or more, 1 must be specified, so use the IF s=
tatement to divide the cases. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> T=
he calculation formula that incorporates the IF statement is</font><br>
			<div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"743327" _msthash=3D"37">
			IF(EXP(-4.6*(J5-1))&gt;1,1,EXP(-4.6*(J5-1)))
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"20150260" _msthash=3D"38"=
> It comes to. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> Calculate the fractal adaptive moving average i=
n column L. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> The fractal adaptiv=
e moving average is the middle value until 1~M-1 day, and the fractal adapt=
ive moving average is after that.<br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"=
> </font><div class=3D"excelformula" _msttexthash=3D"821561" _msthash=3D"39=
">
			=3DIF(ROW()-ROW($L$4)&lt;$L$4,F5,L4+(F5-L4)*K5)
			</div><font _mstmutation=3D"1" _msttexthash=3D"8589971" _msthash=3D"40">=
 It comes to. <br _mstmutation=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> <br _mstmutation=
=3D"1" _istranslated=3D"1"> If you copy the F5~L5 cell and paste it into th=
e cell below F6, you can calculate the fractal adaptive moving average.</fo=
nt><br>
